A||||1||Orlando||Sunroof
Z||000000||Orlando||07-25-99||03:36 PM||||Has anyone ever tried to install a non-factory sunroof in a Fiero? When my car (88 Formula) sits out in the mornin dew, I can see an outline of where the factory sunroof should be. I had an 86 GT with a sunroof, and just about every other factory option there was (even the sub woofer), until some idiot cut in front of me and that was it. I miss the sunroof, and would consider putting in an aftermarket piece. Any stories?
Z||000001||Carrolles||07-30-99||01:05 PM||||All Fieros have the cutout in the metal roof panel for the sunroof (VistaVent).  It would be hard to find an aftermarket one that matched the hole exactly.  You wouldn't want to just attach a smaller one to the plastic roof panel.<br>Ed Parks (FieroFactory@juno.com) has roof panels of most colors that you could swap into your car.<p>
